{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"call_245e455ff3124a2a90d5f46e","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t# Epic 1: Connector Core — Test Plan\n2\t\n3\t**Status:** Draft for review\n4\t**Tech design:** `tech-design.md`\n5\t**Epic:** `epic.md`\n6\t\n7\tThis plan maps every TC to one or more tests, assigns each to a chunk, and lays out the Red/Green sequence per chunk. The mock boundary is fixed by the tech design: the PI hook surface (fed by synthetic events and recorded corpora) and the `ModelCall` (a deterministic fake) are the only external edges; everything LHC runs real against a temp SQLite thread. Connector modules are exercised through their entry points, never mocked against each other.\n8\t\n9\t---\n10\t\n11\t## Test Count Reconciliation\n12\t\n13\t| Chunk | Story | TCs covered | TC tests | Architecture-risk tests | Fixture/foundation tests | Chunk total |\n14\t|-------|-------|-------------|----------|-------------------------|--------------------------|-------------|\n15\t| 0 | Foundation | — | 0 | 0 | 7 | 7 |\n16\t| 1 | Lifecycle | TC-1.1…1.7 | 7 | 1 (restart) | 0 | 8 |\n17\t| 2 | Capture | TC-2.1…2.9 | 9 | 2 (idempotency, atomicity) | 0 | 11 |\n18\t| 3 | Verification | TC-6.1…6.3 | 3 | 1 (fixture validity) | 0 | 4 |\n19\t| 4 | Fork | TC-3.1…3.3 | 3 | 1 (source vs derived) | 0 | 4 |\n20\t| 5 | Inference | TC-4.1…4.5 | 5 | 2 (adapter boundary, concurrency) | 0 | 7 |\n21\t| 6 | Validation | TC-5.1…5.6 | 6 | 0 | 0 | 6 |\n22\t| **Total** | | **33 TCs** | **33** | **7** | **7** | **47** |\n23\t\n24\tCross-checks: 33 TC tests = the 33 TCs in the epic traceability table (one test minimum per TC). 7 architecture-risk tests = the 7 rows in the tech design's Architecture-Risk table. 7 foundation tests = Chunk 0's fixture/smoke/gate invariants, including package verification-script availability. Per-chunk totals sum to 47; the epic's story estimate range (59–74) is wider because it counts finer-grained sub-cases the implementer adds at Green — this plan counts the floor (one test per TC + named risk/foundation tests), not the ceiling.\n25\t\n26\t---\n27\t\n28\t## TC → Test Mapping\n29\t\n30\tGrouped by test file, since each row becomes a Red-phase test. All paths under `packages/pi-lhc/`.\n31\t\n32\t### `test/lifecycle/instance.test.ts`\n33\t\n34\t| TC | Test | Setup | Assert |\n35\t|----|------|-------|--------|\n36\t| TC-1.1 | New launch (no flag) creates one background instance + registered thread | `launch={}`, temp registry+dir | one thread file exists; registry row carries cwd; `resolve` returns it; instance in background mode; queue not driven by connector |\n37\t| TC-1.4 | Shutdown disposes with flush; re-resolved thread complete | capture N events, then `session_shutdown` | re-resolving the thread reads all N events through last pre-shutdown event; no trailing loss |\n38\t\n39\t### `test/lifecycle/thread-resolution.test.ts`\n40\t\n41\t| TC | Test | Setup | Assert |\n42\t|----|------|-------|--------|\n43\t| TC-1.2 | Resolved launch attaches existing thread; no second thread | a registered thread; `launch={session:id}` | `threads.resolve` returns the same threadId; thread count unchanged |\n44\t| TC-1.3 | Plain-data holder survives context replacement | fire two hooks with different `ctx` objects | capture continues using fresh ctx; holder never references a prior ctx (asserted by shape) |\n45\t| TC-1.5 *(risk: restart)* | Reload re-resolves the thread by id after holder discarded | create, **discard in-memory holder**, fire `session_start{reload}` | thread reference rebuilt by resolving the id from the registry; capture continues on same thread |\n46\t| TC-1.6 | Launch modes resolve correctly | `launch` = `{}` / `{session:fullId}` / `{session:partialId}` / `{continue:true}` / `{session:badId}` | new creates; full+partial id resolve the right thread; continue resolves most-recent; bad id returns an actionable error and creates **no** thread |\n47\t| TC-1.7 | `--resume` picker lists cwd-scoped, resolves selection, empty-safe | threads in two cwds; `launch={resume:true}` | list shows only current-cwd threads with title+created; selection resolves; empty cwd returns null, no failure |\n48\t\n49\t### `test/capture/converter.test.ts`\n50\t\n51\t| TC | Test | Setup | Assert |\n52\t|----|------|-------|--------|\n53\t| TC-2.1 | User/assistant/toolResult record ordered; assistant fans out thinking→text→toolCall | synthetic sequence | events recorded in source order; assistant fan-out order exact |\n54\t| TC-2.8 *(risk: atomicity)* | Malformed→gap vs store-unavailable→health signal | (a) malformed on writable thread; (b) unavailable store | (a) durable queryable gap; (b) extension health signal in `SessionState.health`, no gap, no hook exception |\n55\t| TC-2.9 | Model/thinking changes captured as ordered runtime_notes | fire `model_select` then `thinking_level_select` mid-sequence | each records one `runtime_note` carrying new+previous value; order preserved relative to surrounding messages |\n56\t\n57\t### `test/capture/turn-derivation.test.ts`\n58\t\n59\t| TC | Test | Setup | Assert |\n60\t|----|------|-------|--------|\n61\t| TC-2.2 | One-prompt-two-tools-then-answer → exactly one LHC turn, `turn_end` at agent_end | the Flow 2 worked-example corpus | exactly one `turn_end`; emitted at `agent_end`; per-step PI `turn_end`s produce none |\n62\t| TC-2.3 | Session order from converter source-event order, not turnIndex | two agent runs each starting turnIndex 0 | turns ordered by source-event order through the converter; no collision from repeated turnIndex 0 |\n63\t\n64\t### `test/capture/parallel-and-errors.test.ts`\n65\t\n66\t| TC | Test | Setup | Assert |\n67\t|----|------|-------|--------|\n68\t| TC-2.4 | Parallel tool calls, out-of-order completion, correlate by id | assistant with toolCalls a,b; results arrive b,a | each `tool_result` correlated to its call by `toolCallId`, not arrival order |\n69\t| TC-2.5 | Error tool result captured with flag + content | toolResult `isError:true` | `tool_result` event with error flag and content; nothing dropped |\n70\t| TC-2.7 *(risk: idempotency)* | Re-delivered event dedups; normal resume re-fires nothing | replay same event twice; separately, resume | re-delivery returns `skipped`/`duplicate_idempotency_key`; resume produces no historical re-fire |\n71\t\n72\t### `test/capture/abort.test.ts`\n73\t\n74\t| TC | Test | Setup | Assert |\n75\t|----|------|-------|--------|\n76\t| TC-2.6 | Graceful interrupt: partial content + aborted disposition; turn closes complete-but-aborted | aborted-turn corpus (`stopReason:aborted`, agent_end fires) | partial assistant content recorded; aborted disposition carried; turn closed at agent_end |\n77\t\n78\t> Hard-kill (no `agent_end`) is covered as a deterministic-boundary golden in `turn-derivation.test.ts`: open turn left open, tolerated as a no-op on reattach (no duplication of the recorded prefix).\n79\t\n80\t### `test/lifecycle/fork.test.ts`\n81\t\n82\t| TC | Test | Setup | Assert |\n83\t|----|------|-------|--------|\n84\t| TC-3.1 *(risk: source-vs-derived)* | Fork creates new thread; source receives no writes | capture a thread, fork it | new thread created; source **logical read-back** (events/messages/turns) unchanged; fork point resolved from `session_before_fork` hook (PI session tree as Epic-1 fallback) |\n85\t| TC-3.2 | Fork seeded by replay; read-back matches source through fork point | fork at a known entry | seeded thread read-back equals source read-back through the fork point |\n86\t| TC-3.3 | Forms requeue on fork (v1: no copy) | fork a thread with ready forms | target's forms requeue and drain; not copied from source |\n87\t\n88\t### `test/inference/model-call.test.ts`\n89\t\n90\t| TC | Test | Setup | Assert |\n91\t|----|------|-------|--------|\n92\t| TC-4.1 | Function resolves (provider,model) via registry, returns text | fake registry + complete returning text | returns `{ok:true,text}` for a single-turn message list |\n93\t| TC-4.2 | Two kinds → different (provider,model) both route in one session | two assignments, two fakes | each call routes by its keys; both succeed |\n94\t| TC-4.3 *(risk: adapter boundary)* | Failure shapes map to exact kinds | inject auth, invalid-request, rate-limit, timeout, network, thrown | terminal: auth, invalid_request; retryable: rate_limit, timeout, network; thrown → other |\n95\t| TC-4.4 | Resolved-but-no-output → `empty_output` by adapter (not host fn) | complete returns empty content | LHC adapter yields `empty_output`; host fn returns text-or-transport-failure only |\n96\t\n97\t### `test/inference/closed-loop.test.ts`\n98\t\n99\t| TC | Test | Setup | Assert |\n100\t|----|------|-------|--------|\n101\t| TC-4.5 | Captured thread's queued derivation invokes fn + persists outcome | captured thread; fakes (one text, one failure); `drainSettled` | at least one ready derived form + one classified failure, both queryable via inspect/health |\n102\t| *(risk: concurrency)* | Stale background result does not clobber newer state | force a stale derivation result against advanced state | newer state wins; stale result discarded |\n103\t\n104\t### `test/inference/startup-validation.test.ts`\n105\t\n106\t| TC | Test | Setup | Assert |\n107\t|----|------|-------|--------|\n108\t| TC-5.1 | All seven assignments validated against registry before first use | seven assignments, registry | validation runs at session start, before any derivation |\n109\t| TC-5.2 | Unreachable lane reported with kind+pair+fix; appears headless | two assignments: (a) `modelRegistry.find(provider, model)` fails; (b) model exists but `hasConfiguredAuth(model)`/`getAvailable()` says auth is absent; headless mode (`hasUI:false`) | report names kind, (provider,model), reason, and distinct fix (`fix assignment` vs `run login/configure auth`); emitted via headless channel and stored in `SessionState.health`, not only TUI |\n110\t| TC-5.3 | Validation failure leaves capture running | an unreachable lane | capture continues; affected lane's derivations fail classified + queryable |\n111\t\n112\t### `test/inference/assignments.test.ts`\n113\t\n114\t| TC | Test | Setup | Assert |\n115\t|----|------|-------|--------|\n116\t| TC-5.4 | Seven kinds load (provider,model,prompt) with shipped defaults; prompt registered | default config | all seven resolve; each prompt names a registered prompt |\n117\t| TC-5.5 | Override takes effect next start, no code change | config override one kind | next `session_start` uses the override |\n118\t| TC-5.6 | Incomplete/unknown assignment fails loud at init | missing kind / unknown prompt / placeholder | construction throws actionable error; no placeholder masks it |\n119\t\n120\t### `test/verify/replay.test.ts`\n121\t\n122\t| TC | Test | Setup | Assert |\n123\t|----|------|-------|--------|\n124\t| TC-6.1 | Each corpus replays to a thread whose read-back matches the fixture | chatty, tool-heavy, parallel, error, aborted corpora | read-back (events/messages/turns) matches fixture expectation per corpus |\n125\t| TC-6.2 | Same corpus replayed twice → identical read-back | one corpus, two replays | byte-identical read-back; IDs and order stable |\n126\t| TC-6.3 | inspect overview/health reflect captured session | a captured thread with a gap + a failed form | counts, last position, gaps, failed derivations all visible |\n127\t\n128\t### `test/fixtures/corpus.test.ts` *(risk: fixture validity)*\n129\t\n130\t| Test | Assert |\n131\t|------|--------|\n132\t| Corpus loader yields valid MessageEventInput shapes + lifecycle-coherent sequences | every loaded corpus parses to well-formed events; named invalid builder produces the intended malformed shape |\n133\t\n134\t---\n135\t\n136\t## Per-Chunk Red/Green Sequence\n137\t\n138\tEach chunk: write skeletons (structured-result stubs for services/adapters/handlers; `NotImplementedError` for pure algorithms) → Red (tests written, failing for the right reason — never asserting on `NotImplementedError`) → Green (implement to pass). Exit each chunk on `green-verify`.\n139\t\n140\t### Chunk 0: Foundation\n141\t\n142\t- **Skeleton:** all interface exports (`tech-design.md` → Interface Definitions); `index.ts` hook registration with stubbed handlers; `state.ts` complete (plain data, no stub).\n143\t- **Red:** fixture-invariant tests (corpus shapes, synthetic coherence, temp-thread create+reopen); extension-loads smoke; package verification scripts/config present.\n144\t- **Green:** fixtures + loaders + temp-thread factory implemented; extension registers hooks; `red-verify`/`verify`/`green-verify`/`verify-all` scripts run.\n145\t- **Exit:** `red-verify` green; 7 foundation tests pass.\n146\t\n147\t### Chunk 1: Lifecycle\n148\t\n149\t- **Skeleton:** `instance.ts`, `thread-resolution.ts`, `picker.ts` as structured-result stubs.\n150\t- **Red:** TC-1.1–1.7 + restart risk test, failing.\n151\t- **Green:** construct/dispose, launch resolution (new / `--session` partial-id / `--continue` / `--resume` picker), reload re-resolution, plain-data enforcement.\n152\t- **Exit:** `green-verify`; 8 tests pass.\n153\t\n154\t### Chunk 2: Capture\n155\t\n156\t- **Skeleton:** `map-message.ts`, `turn-accumulator.ts`, `idempotency.ts` (`NotImplementedError`); `converter.ts` (structured result).\n157\t- **Red:** TC-2.1–2.9 + idempotency + atomicity risk tests, failing. Turn-derivation goldens (worked example, abort, hard-kill) written here.\n158\t- **Green:** mapping fan-out, turn accumulation, runtime-change capture (model/thinking → runtime_note), key construction, batch flush with failure isolation.\n159\t- **Exit:** `green-verify`; 11 tests pass. Highest-risk chunk — turn derivation and dedup are the load-bearing mechanics.\n160\t\n161\t### Chunk 3: Verification\n162\t\n163\t- **Skeleton:** `verify/replay.ts` (structured compare).\n164\t- **Red:** TC-6.1–6.3 + fixture-validity risk test, failing.\n165\t- **Green:** replay through the real converter+intake path; read-back compare; inspect surfacing.\n166\t- **Exit:** `green-verify`; 4 tests pass. Consumes M0 corpora; widens as they arrive.\n167\t\n168\t### Chunk 4: Fork\n169\t\n170\t- **Skeleton:** `fork.ts` (detect + seed, structured result).\n171\t- **Red:** TC-3.1–3.3 + source-vs-derived risk test, failing.\n172\t- **Green:** fork-point detection (`session_before_fork` hook; PI session tree as Epic-1 fallback), replay-seed, requeue, source read-only.\n173\t- **Exit:** `green-verify`; 4 tests pass.\n174\t\n175\t### Chunk 5: Inference\n176\t\n177\t- **Skeleton:** `model-call.ts` (`createModelCall`, `classifyFailure`).\n178\t- **Red:** TC-4.1–4.5 + adapter-boundary + concurrency risk tests, failing. TC-4.5 uses captured content from Chunk 2 + real scheduler + `drainSettled`.\n179\t- **Green:** registry resolve + complete, classification, multi-lane, closed-loop wiring.\n180\t- **Exit:** `green-verify`; 7 tests pass.\n181\t\n182\t### Chunk 6: Validation\n183\t\n184\t- **Skeleton:** `assignments.ts`, `startup-validation.ts`.\n185\t- **Red:** TC-5.1–5.6, failing.\n186\t- **Green:** shape validation (LHC-enforced at construction) + reachability probe through `modelRegistry.find` plus configured-auth check + `ctx.ui`/headless reporting + override.\n187\t- **Exit:** `green-verify`; 6 tests pass.\n188\t\n189\t---\n190\t\n191\t## Suite Accounting\n192\t\n193\t| Suite | Status | Note |\n194\t|-------|--------|------|\n195\t| `vitest run` (unit + entry-point) | ran | the 44 tests above |\n196\t| `red-verify` (build/typecheck/lint/boundaries) | ran | per chunk |\n197\t| `check-test-immutability` | ran | Green exit |\n198\t| integration / e2e | **absent** | no separate suite this epic; `verify-all` == `verify` |\n199\t| Manual: load into real PI, run a session, inspect | manual | the wide pass; not automated, recorded in tech-design Testing Strategy |\n200\t\n201\tNo suite is skipped on auth availability — the closed-loop test (TC-4.5) uses a deterministic `ModelCall` fake, not a live provider, so it always runs.\n202\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"a7689c21-1739-4f71-b1a5-e967f006f0f9","uuid":"573c2a59-006c-4115-adda-20685b55c39d","timestamp":"2026-06-14T13:45:51.829Z","tool_use_result":{"type":"text","file":{"filePath":"/Users/leemoore/code/pi-long-horizon/liminal-context/docs/specs/02-pi-lhc/01-connector-core/test-plan.md","content":"# Epic 1: Connector Core — Test Plan\n\n**Status:** Draft for review\n**Tech design:** `tech-design.md`\n**Epic:** `epic.md`\n\nThis plan maps every TC to one or more tests, assigns each to a chunk, and lays out the Red/Green sequence per chunk. The mock boundary is fixed by the tech design: the PI hook surface (fed by synthetic events and recorded corpora) and the `ModelCall` (a deterministic fake) are the only external edges; everything LHC runs real against a temp SQLite thread. Connector modules are exercised through their entry points, never mocked against each other.\n\n---\n\n## Test Count Reconciliation\n\n| Chunk | Story | TCs covered | TC tests | Architecture-risk tests | Fixture/foundation tests | Chunk total |\n|-------|-------|-------------|----------|-------------------------|--------------------------|-------------|\n| 0 | Foundation | — | 0 | 0 | 7 | 7 |\n| 1 | Lifecycle | TC-1.1…1.7 | 7 | 1 (restart) | 0 | 8 |\n| 2 | Capture | TC-2.1…2.9 | 9 | 2 (idempotency, atomicity) | 0 | 11 |\n| 3 | Verification | TC-6.1…6.3 | 3 | 1 (fixture validity) | 0 | 4 |\n| 4 | Fork | TC-3.1…3.3 | 3 | 1 (source vs derived) | 0 | 4 |\n| 5 | Inference | TC-4.1…4.5 | 5 | 2 (adapter boundary, concurrency) | 0 | 7 |\n| 6 | Validation | TC-5.1…5.6 | 6 | 0 | 0 | 6 |\n| **Total** | | **33 TCs** | **33** | **7** | **7** | **47** |\n\nCross-checks: 33 TC tests = the 33 TCs in the epic traceability table (one test minimum per TC). 7 architecture-risk tests = the 7 rows in the tech design's Architecture-Risk table. 7 foundation tests = Chunk 0's fixture/smoke/gate invariants, including package verification-script availability. Per-chunk totals sum to 47; the epic's story estimate range (59–74) is wider because it counts finer-grained sub-cases the implementer adds at Green — this plan counts the floor (one test per TC + named risk/foundation tests), not the ceiling.\n\n---\n\n## TC → Test Mapping\n\nGrouped by test file, since each row becomes a Red-phase test. All paths under `packages/pi-lhc/`.\n\n### `test/lifecycle/instance.test.ts`\n\n| TC | Test | Setup | Assert |\n|----|------|-------|--------|\n| TC-1.1 | New launch (no flag) creates one background instance + registered thread | `launch={}`, temp registry+dir | one thread file exists; registry row carries cwd; `resolve` returns it; instance in background mode; queue not driven by connector |\n| TC-1.4 | Shutdown disposes with flush; re-resolved thread complete | capture N events, then `session_shutdown` | re-resolving the thread reads all N events through last pre-shutdown event; no trailing loss |\n\n### `test/lifecycle/thread-resolution.test.ts`\n\n| TC | Test | Setup | Assert |\n|----|------|-------|--------|\n| TC-1.2 | Resolved launch attaches existing thread; no second thread | a registered thread; `launch={session:id}` | `threads.resolve` returns the same threadId; thread count unchanged |\n| TC-1.3 | Plain-data holder survives context replacement | fire two hooks with different `ctx` objects | capture continues using fresh ctx; holder never references a prior ctx (asserted by shape) |\n| TC-1.5 *(risk: restart)* | Reload re-resolves the thread by id after holder discarded | create, **discard in-memory holder**, fire `session_start{reload}` | thread reference rebuilt by resolving the id from the registry; capture continues on same thread |\n| TC-1.6 | Launch modes resolve correctly | `launch` = `{}` / `{session:fullId}` / `{session:partialId}` / `{continue:true}` / `{session:badId}` | new creates; full+partial id resolve the right thread; continue resolves most-recent; bad id returns an actionable error and creates **no** thread |\n| TC-1.7 | `--resume` picker lists cwd-scoped, resolves selection, empty-safe | threads in two cwds; `launch={resume:true}` | list shows only current-cwd threads with title+created; selection resolves; empty cwd returns null, no failure |\n\n### `test/capture/converter.test.ts`\n\n| TC | Test | Setup | Assert |\n|----|------|-------|--------|\n| TC-2.1 | User/assistant/toolResult record ordered; assistant fans out thinking→text→toolCall | synthetic sequence | events recorded in source order; assistant fan-out order exact |\n| TC-2.8 *(risk: atomicity)* | Malformed→gap vs store-unavailable→health signal | (a) malformed on writable thread; (b) unavailable store | (a) durable queryable gap; (b) extension health signal in `SessionState.health`, no gap, no hook exception |\n| TC-2.9 | Model/thinking changes captured as ordered runtime_notes | fire `model_select` then `thinking_level_select` mid-sequence | each records one `runtime_note` carrying new+previous value; order preserved relative to surrounding messages |\n\n### `test/capture/turn-derivation.test.ts`\n\n| TC | Test | Setup | Assert |\n|----|------|-------|--------|\n| TC-2.2 | One-prompt-two-tools-then-answer → exactly one LHC turn, `turn_end` at agent_end | the Flow 2 worked-example corpus | exactly one `turn_end`; emitted at `agent_end`; per-step PI `turn_end`s produce none |\n| TC-2.3 | Session order from converter source-event order, not turnIndex | two agent runs each starting turnIndex 0 | turns ordered by source-event order through the converter; no collision from repeated turnIndex 0 |\n\n### `test/capture/parallel-and-errors.test.ts`\n\n| TC | Test | Setup | Assert |\n|----|------|-------|--------|\n| TC-2.4 | Parallel tool calls, out-of-order completion, correlate by id | assistant with toolCalls a,b; results arrive b,a | each `tool_result` correlated to its call by `toolCallId`, not arrival order |\n| TC-2.5 | Error tool result captured with flag + content | toolResult `isError:true` | `tool_result` event with error flag and content; nothing dropped |\n| TC-2.7 *(risk: idempotency)* | Re-delivered event dedups; normal resume re-fires nothing | replay same event twice; separately, resume | re-delivery returns `skipped`/`duplicate_idempotency_key`; resume produces no historical re-fire |\n\n### `test/capture/abort.test.ts`\n\n| TC | Test | Setup | Assert |\n|----|------|-------|--------|\n| TC-2.6 | Graceful interrupt: partial content + aborted disposition; turn closes complete-but-aborted | aborted-turn corpus (`stopReason:aborted`, agent_end fires) | partial assistant content recorded; aborted disposition carried; turn closed at agent_end |\n\n> Hard-kill (no `agent_end`) is covered as a deterministic-boundary golden in `turn-derivation.test.ts`: open turn left open, tolerated as a no-op on reattach (no duplication of the recorded prefix).\n\n### `test/lifecycle/fork.test.ts`\n\n| TC | Test | Setup | Assert |\n|----|------|-------|--------|\n| TC-3.1 *(risk: source-vs-derived)* | Fork creates new thread; source receives no writes | capture a thread, fork it | new thread created; source **logical read-back** (events/messages/turns) unchanged; fork point resolved from `session_before_fork` hook (PI session tree as Epic-1 fallback) |\n| TC-3.2 | Fork seeded by replay; read-back matches source through fork point | fork at a known entry | seeded thread read-back equals source read-back through the fork point |\n| TC-3.3 | Forms requeue on fork (v1: no copy) | fork a thread with ready forms | target's forms requeue and drain; not copied from source |\n\n### `test/inference/model-call.test.ts`\n\n| TC | Test | Setup | Assert |\n|----|------|-------|--------|\n| TC-4.1 | Function resolves (provider,model) via registry, returns text | fake registry + complete returning text | returns `{ok:true,text}` for a single-turn message list |\n| TC-4.2 | Two kinds → different (provider,model) both route in one session | two assignments, two fakes | each call routes by its keys; both succeed |\n| TC-4.3 *(risk: adapter boundary)* | Failure shapes map to exact kinds | inject auth, invalid-request, rate-limit, timeout, network, thrown | terminal: auth, invalid_request; retryable: rate_limit, timeout, network; thrown → other |\n| TC-4.4 | Resolved-but-no-output → `empty_output` by adapter (not host fn) | complete returns empty content | LHC adapter yields `empty_output`; host fn returns text-or-transport-failure only |\n\n### `test/inference/closed-loop.test.ts`\n\n| TC | Test | Setup | Assert |\n|----|------|-------|--------|\n| TC-4.5 | Captured thread's queued derivation invokes fn + persists outcome | captured thread; fakes (one text, one failure); `drainSettled` | at least one ready derived form + one classified failure, both queryable via inspect/health |\n| *(risk: concurrency)* | Stale background result does not clobber newer state | force a stale derivation result against advanced state | newer state wins; stale result discarded |\n\n### `test/inference/startup-validation.test.ts`\n\n| TC | Test | Setup | Assert |\n|----|------|-------|--------|\n| TC-5.1 | All seven assignments validated against registry before first use | seven assignments, registry | validation runs at session start, before any derivation |\n| TC-5.2 | Unreachable lane reported with kind+pair+fix; appears headless | two assignments: (a) `modelRegistry.find(provider, model)` fails; (b) model exists but `hasConfiguredAuth(model)`/`getAvailable()` says auth is absent; headless mode (`hasUI:false`) | report names kind, (provider,model), reason, and distinct fix (`fix assignment` vs `run login/configure auth`); emitted via headless channel and stored in `SessionState.health`, not only TUI |\n| TC-5.3 | Validation failure leaves capture running | an unreachable lane | capture continues; affected lane's derivations fail classified + queryable |\n\n### `test/inference/assignments.test.ts`\n\n| TC | Test | Setup | Assert |\n|----|------|-------|--------|\n| TC-5.4 | Seven kinds load (provider,model,prompt) with shipped defaults; prompt registered | default config | all seven resolve; each prompt names a registered prompt |\n| TC-5.5 | Override takes effect next start, no code change | config override one kind | next `session_start` uses the override |\n| TC-5.6 | Incomplete/unknown assignment fails loud at init | missing kind / unknown prompt / placeholder | construction throws actionable error; no placeholder masks it |\n\n### `test/verify/replay.test.ts`\n\n| TC | Test | Setup | Assert |\n|----|------|-------|--------|\n| TC-6.1 | Each corpus replays to a thread whose read-back matches the fixture | chatty, tool-heavy, parallel, error, aborted corpora | read-back (events/messages/turns) matches fixture expectation per corpus |\n| TC-6.2 | Same corpus replayed twice → identical read-back | one corpus, two replays | byte-identical read-back; IDs and order stable |\n| TC-6.3 | inspect overview/health reflect captured session | a captured thread with a gap + a failed form | counts, last position, gaps, failed derivations all visible |\n\n### `test/fixtures/corpus.test.ts` *(risk: fixture validity)*\n\n| Test | Assert |\n|------|--------|\n| Corpus loader yields valid MessageEventInput shapes + lifecycle-coherent sequences | every loaded corpus parses to well-formed events; named invalid builder produces the intended malformed shape |\n\n---\n\n## Per-Chunk Red/Green Sequence\n\nEach chunk: write skeletons (structured-result stubs for services/adapters/handlers; `NotImplementedError` for pure algorithms) → Red (tests written, failing for the right reason — never asserting on `NotImplementedError`) → Green (implement to pass). Exit each chunk on `green-verify`.\n\n### Chunk 0: Foundation\n\n- **Skeleton:** all interface exports (`tech-design.md` → Interface Definitions); `index.ts` hook registration with stubbed handlers; `state.ts` complete (plain data, no stub).\n- **Red:** fixture-invariant tests (corpus shapes, synthetic coherence, temp-thread create+reopen); extension-loads smoke; package verification scripts/config present.\n- **Green:** fixtures + loaders + temp-thread factory implemented; extension registers hooks; `red-verify`/`verify`/`green-verify`/`verify-all` scripts run.\n- **Exit:** `red-verify` green; 7 foundation tests pass.\n\n### Chunk 1: Lifecycle\n\n- **Skeleton:** `instance.ts`, `thread-resolution.ts`, `picker.ts` as structured-result stubs.\n- **Red:** TC-1.1–1.7 + restart risk test, failing.\n- **Green:** construct/dispose, launch resolution (new / `--session` partial-id / `--continue` / `--resume` picker), reload re-resolution, plain-data enforcement.\n- **Exit:** `green-verify`; 8 tests pass.\n\n### Chunk 2: Capture\n\n- **Skeleton:** `map-message.ts`, `turn-accumulator.ts`, `idempotency.ts` (`NotImplementedError`); `converter.ts` (structured result).\n- **Red:** TC-2.1–2.9 + idempotency + atomicity risk tests, failing. Turn-derivation goldens (worked example, abort, hard-kill) written here.\n- **Green:** mapping fan-out, turn accumulation, runtime-change capture (model/thinking → runtime_note), key construction, batch flush with failure isolation.\n- **Exit:** `green-verify`; 11 tests pass. Highest-risk chunk — turn derivation and dedup are the load-bearing mechanics.\n\n### Chunk 3: Verification\n\n- **Skeleton:** `verify/replay.ts` (structured compare).\n- **Red:** TC-6.1–6.3 + fixture-validity risk test, failing.\n- **Green:** replay through the real converter+intake path; read-back compare; inspect surfacing.\n- **Exit:** `green-verify`; 4 tests pass. Consumes M0 corpora; widens as they arrive.\n\n### Chunk 4: Fork\n\n- **Skeleton:** `fork.ts` (detect + seed, structured result).\n- **Red:** TC-3.1–3.3 + source-vs-derived risk test, failing.\n- **Green:** fork-point detection (`session_before_fork` hook; PI session tree as Epic-1 fallback), replay-seed, requeue, source read-only.\n- **Exit:** `green-verify`; 4 tests pass.\n\n### Chunk 5: Inference\n\n- **Skeleton:** `model-call.ts` (`createModelCall`, `classifyFailure`).\n- **Red:** TC-4.1–4.5 + adapter-boundary + concurrency risk tests, failing. TC-4.5 uses captured content from Chunk 2 + real scheduler + `drainSettled`.\n- **Green:** registry resolve + complete, classification, multi-lane, closed-loop wiring.\n- **Exit:** `green-verify`; 7 tests pass.\n\n### Chunk 6: Validation\n\n- **Skeleton:** `assignments.ts`, `startup-validation.ts`.\n- **Red:** TC-5.1–5.6, failing.\n- **Green:** shape validation (LHC-enforced at construction) + reachability probe through `modelRegistry.find` plus configured-auth check + `ctx.ui`/headless reporting + override.\n- **Exit:** `green-verify`; 6 tests pass.\n\n---\n\n## Suite Accounting\n\n| Suite | Status | Note |\n|-------|--------|------|\n| `vitest run` (unit + entry-point) | ran | the 44 tests above |\n| `red-verify` (build/typecheck/lint/boundaries) | ran | per chunk |\n| `check-test-immutability` | ran | Green exit |\n| integration / e2e | **absent** | no separate suite this epic; `verify-all` == `verify` |\n| Manual: load into real PI, run a session, inspect | manual | the wide pass; not automated, recorded in tech-design Testing Strategy |\n\nNo suite is skipped on auth availability — the closed-loop test (TC-4.5) uses a deterministic `ModelCall` fake, not a live provider, so it always runs.\n","numLines":202,"startLine":1,"totalLines":202}}}
{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"call_715b365ca17645009ab937d9","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t{\"command\":\"epic-review\",\"version\":1,\"status\":\"blocked\",\"outcome\":\"block\",\"result\":{\"outcome\":\"block\",\"canonicalReview\":{\"outcome\":\"block\",\"reviewerLabels\":[\"epic-reviewer-1\",\"epic-reviewer-2\"],\"reconciliationSummary\":\"Reviewer-1 assessed the epic as complete with three non-blocking observations about documented limitations. Reviewer-2 identified two major blocking findings (EV-001, EV-002) concerning Story 1 thread identity on reload and --resume operator selection. Both findings are supported by code evidence: the implementation explicitly acknowledges cwd-most-recent reload reattach as an Epic-1 convenience with concurrent same-cwd limitations (thread-resolution.ts:118-121) and most-recent auto-selection as a spec deviation due to PI's lack of interactive input (index.ts:181-190). The Story 1 verification artifact (014-verify.json) confirms both SV-001 and SV-002 are 'needs-human-ruling' with gates passing but production behavior deviating from literal AC requirements. Because Reviewer-2 returned block and the deviations are acknowledged in-code with no human-ruling accepting them, the conservative position preserves the block.\",\"crossStoryFindings\":[\"Cross-story consistency is strong across Stories 2-6. The plain-data-only rule (AC-1.3) is consistently enforced — only SessionState is retained across hooks, no PI context objects.\",\"Turn derivation logic is consistent throughout — turn_end events are emitted only at agent_end, ignoring PI's per-step turn_end boundaries (AC-2.2).\",\"Idempotency key construction uses the same tiered approach (entryId → toolCallId → responseId → fallback) across capture, replay, and fork paths (AC-2.6).\",\"Module boundaries are clean: lifecycle, capture, inference, and verify surfaces maintain separation of concerns with no internal module mocking.\"],\"architectureFindings\":[\"Implementation closely follows the tech design's module architecture. The hook rail in index.ts correctly routes to appropriate handlers.\",\"The converter is properly decomposed into map-message (pure), turn-accumulator (state machine), idempotency (pure), and converter (orchestration) as designed.\",\"Capture failure isolation matches the design contract: writable thread failures produce durable gaps via runtime_note events; store-unavailable failures surface as health signals (AC-2.7).\",\"Inference routing correctly treats provider/model as opaque routing keys, with real PI model registry resolution via dynamic import.\",\"Fork implementation follows the Epic 1 design: detection via session_before_fork hook with PI session tree fallback, seeding by event replay, source thread immutability verified (AC-3.1, AC-3.2).\",\"The two blocking deviations are acknowledged design positions taken in Epic 1 as conveniences pending Feature 2+ permanent lineage metadata.\"],\"epicCoverageAssessment\":[\"Story 0 (Foundation): Complete — extension loads, registers Epic 1 observe-only hook rail, plain-data state holder established, fixture infrastructure in place.\",\"Story 1 (Lifecycle): Complete with acknowledged deviations — instance init/dispose with flush, thread resolution by launch mode (new/--session/--continue), reload reconstruction uses cwd-most-recent for no-flag/--resume (SV-001 documented deviation), cwd-scoped picker with most-recent auto-selection (SV-002 documented deviation).\",\"Story 2 (Capture): Complete — PI→LHC event mapping with content-part fan-out, turn derivation (one LHC turn per agent run), parallel tool correlation by toolCallId, error-result capture, graceful abort handling, runtime-change capture, idempotency-keyed dedup, capture-failure isolation (AC-2.1 through AC-2.8).\",\"Story 3 (Verification): Complete — corpus replay through real converter, read-back comparison against fixtures, deterministic replay verified, inspect overview/health surfaces (AC-6.1 through AC-6.3).\",\"Story 4 (Fork): Complete — fork detection (hook + PI session tree fallback), new thread seeded by replay to fork point, source thread immutability verified, derived forms requeue (AC-3.1 through AC-3.3).\",\"Story 5 (Inference): Complete — ModelCall function over PI model registry, multi-lane routing, provider-error classification (auth/invalid_request terminal, rate_limit/timeout/network retryable, thrown→other), empty_output handling by LHC adapter (AC-4.1 through AC-4.5).\",\"Story 6 (Validation): Complete — all seven assignments validated against PI registry before first derivation use, unreachable lane reporting with kind+(provider,model)+fix, headless-safe reporting (ctx.ui.notify when available, stderr fallback), capture continues on validation failure (AC-5.1 through AC-5.6).\"],\"productionPathFindings\":[\"Real LHC SDK execution path confirmed — no LHC mocking, all persistence runs against real SQLite temp threads in tests.\",\"Real converter path exercised — mapMessage, TurnAccumulator, and capture functions are production code, not test doubles.\",\"Real fork seeding path — seedFork uses actual intakeStream.messageEvents for replay, not a mock write path.\",\"Real inspect/health surfaces — overview and health reads come from LHC SDK, not faked responses.\",\"PI types deviation is documented and temporary — local declarations in src/pi/types.ts mirror verified v0.79.2 shapes; will swap to real @earendil-works/pi-coding-agent imports when package is installed (Epic 2/4).\",\"pi-ai types deviation is documented and temporary — local declarations in src/inference/pi-ai.ts; production uses dynamic import of @earendil-works/pi-ai with graceful failure when unavailable.\",\"DETERMINED PRODUCTION PATH DEVIATION: Reload for no-flag and --resume uses cwd-most-recent registry selection rather than reconstructing from a prior resolved thread id (EV-001). The implementation acknowledges this as an Epic-1 convenience with concurrent same-cwd limitations.\",\"DETERMINED PRODUCTION PATH DEVIATION: Production --resume presents candidates through ctx.ui.notify but auto-selects most recent thread rather than resolving an explicit operator selection (EV-002). The implementation acknowledges this as a spec deviation due to PI v0.79.2 lacking an interactive input surface.\"],\"blockingFindings\":[{\"id\":\"EV-001\",\"severity\":\"major\",\"title\":\"Reload for no-flag and --resume uses cwd-most-recent registry selection instead of reconstructing from the resolved thread id\",\"evidence\":\"AC-1.5 requires reload reconstruction from 'the resolved thread id' (epic.md:137). resolveReloadThread for no-flag/--resume uses listed.value.at(-1) after threads.listThreads({cwd}) (thread-resolution.ts:141-145). The code comment (lines 118-121) acknowledges this as an Epic-1 convenience with 'known concurrent same-cwd limitation' and defers precise lineage to Feature 2+. The production test (thread-resolution.test.ts:335-370) only proves the single-thread-in-cwd case. Story 1 verification (014-verify.json) confirms SV-001 is 'needs-human-ruling' with gates passing but production behavior deviating from AC-1.5.\",\"affectedFiles\":[\"packages/pi-lhc/src/lifecycle/thread-resolution.ts\",\"packages/pi-lhc/src/index.ts\",\"packages/pi-lhc/test/lifecycle/thread-resolution.test.ts\",\"docs/specs/02-pi-lhc/01-connector-core/artifacts/01-session-lifecycle-and-thread-resolution/014-verify.json\"],\"requirementIds\":[\"AC-1.5\",\"TC-1.5\"],\"recommendedFixScope\":\"human-ruling\",\"blocking\":true},{\"id\":\"EV-002\",\"severity\":\"major\",\"title\":\"Production --resume auto-selects most recent thread instead of resolving an operator selection\",\"evidence\":\"AC-1.7 requires --resume to 'resolve the operator's selection' (epic.md:141). defaultSelectThread (index.ts:191-201) presents candidates via ctx.ui.notify but returns mostRecent.threadId without operator input. The code comment (lines 181-190) acknowledges this as 'a precise spec deviation' because PI v0.79.2 'exposes no interactive input/selection surface'. The production test (thread-resolution.test.ts:255-290) asserts notification plus most-recent behavior as the expected path. Story 1 verification (014-verify.json) confirms SV-002 is 'needs-human-ruling' with gates passing but production behavior deviating from AC-1.7.\",\"affectedFiles\":[\"packages/pi-lhc/src/index.ts\",\"packages/pi-lhc/src/lifecycle/picker.ts\",\"packages/pi-lhc/test/lifecycle/thread-resolution.test.ts\",\"docs/specs/02-pi-lhc/01-connector-core/artifacts/01-session-lifecycle-and-thread-resolution/014-verify.json\"],\"requirementIds\":[\"AC-1.7\",\"TC-1.7\"],\"recommendedFixScope\":\"human-ruling\",\"blocking\":true}],\"nonBlockingFindings\":[{\"id\":\"NF-001\",\"severity\":\"observation\",\"title\":\"Documented idempotency edge case for identity-less events\",\"evidence\":\"Story 2 implementation notes SV-001 residual: a truly identity-less event (no entryId AND no source position AND same content) cannot satisfy both stable-on-redelivery AND unique-per-occurrence constraints. Real PI message_end always carries a stable entry id per research, so this edge is unreachable on the production hook path.\",\"affectedFiles\":[\"packages/pi-lhc/src/capture/idempotency.ts\"],\"requirementIds\":[\"AC-2.6\"],\"recommendedFixScope\":\"human-ruling\",\"blocking\":false},{\"id\":\"NF-002\",\"severity\":\"observation\",\"title\":\"PI extension input/selection API unavailable for --resume picker\",\"evidence\":\"Story 1 implementation notes SV-002: PI v0.79.2 exposes no interactive input/selection surface. Production --resume presents candidates via ctx.ui.notify and auto-selects most-recent. Exact operator selection and exact-prior-thread reload are deferred until PI provides the API. This is the root cause of EV-002.\",\"affectedFiles\":[\"packages/pi-lhc/src/lifecycle/picker.ts\",\"packages/pi-lhc/src/index.ts\"],\"requirementIds\":[\"AC-1.7\"],\"recommendedFixScope\":\"fresh-fix-path\",\"blocking\":false},{\"id\":\"NF-003\",\"severity\":\"observation\",\"title\":\"Derived form reuse optimization deferred for v1\",\"evidence\":\"Story 4 fork implementation always requeues derived forms rather than copying/reusing ready forms. Fork correctness is preserved (AC-3.3 permits reuse 'may'), but provenance-identity safety is not yet implemented. Reuse optimization deferred to Epic 2+.\",\"affectedFiles\":[\"packages/pi-lhc/src/lifecycle/fork.ts\"],\"requirementIds\":[\"AC-3.3\"],\"recommendedFixScope\":\"fresh-fix-path\",\"blocking\":false}],\"unresolvedItems\":[\"Human ruling needed: Accept or reject cwd-most-recent registry reattach as satisfying AC-1.5 for Story 1 despite the known concurrent same-cwd limitation documented in thread-resolution.ts:118-121.\",\"Human ruling needed: Accept or reject notify-list plus most-recent default as satisfying AC-1.7 until PI exposes an interactive selection API, as documented in index.ts:181-190.\",\"M0 corpora for Story 3 fixtures — current implementation uses synthetic builders; test coverage widens when M0 delivers recorded PI sessions.\",\"Image/file-reference handling decision (A-7) — interim implementation degrades unsupported parts to runtime_note events with omission text; safe default that can extend intake schema when M0 decides.\",\"PI extension input/selection API — upstream request filed for real --resume picker and exact-thread reload capability.\",\"createSdk→initLhc rename (A-4) — mechanical rename pending in lhc package; pi-lhc uses initLhc wrapper as documented in tech design.\"],\"gateResult\":\"pass\"},\"verifierResults\":[{\"resultId\":\"50001564-8c3b-4dbe-9b12-32f1a675a326\",\"outcome\":\"pass\",\"provider\":\"claude-code\",\"model\":\"claude-opus-4-8\",\"reviewerLabel\":\"epic-reviewer-1\",\"crossStoryFindings\":[\"Cross-story consistency is strong across the implementation. The plain-data-only rule (AC-1.3) is consistently enforced - only SessionState is retained across hooks, no PI context objects.\",\"Turn derivation logic is consistent throughout - turn_end events are emitted only at agent_end, ignoring PI's per-step turn_end boundaries.\",\"Idempotency key construction uses the same tiered approach (entryId → toolCallId → responseId → fallback) across capture, replay, and fork paths.\",\"Module boundaries are clean and well-respected: lifecycle, capture, inference, and verify surfaces maintain their separation of concerns.\"],\"architectureFindings\":[\"Implementation closely follows the tech design's module architecture. The hook rail in index.ts correctly routes to appropriate handlers.\",\"The converter is properly decomposed into map-message (pure), turn-accumulator (state machine), idempotency (pure), and converter (orchestration) as designed.\",\"Capture failure isolation matches the design contract: writable thread failures produce durable gaps via runtime_note events; store-unavailable failures surface as health signals.\",\"The inference routing correctly treats provider/model as opaque routing keys, with real PI model registry resolution via dynamic import.\",\"Fork implementation follows the Epic 1 design: detection via session_before_fork hook with PI session tree fallback, seeding by event replay, source thread immutability verified.\"],\"epicCoverageAssessment\":[\"Story 0 (Foundation): Complete - extension loads, registers Epic 1 observe-only hook rail, plain-data state holder established, fixture infrastructure in place.\",\"Story 1 (Lifecycle): Complete - instance init/dispose with flush, thread resolution by launch mode (new/--session/--continue), reload reconstruction from durable registry, cwd-scoped picker.\",\"Story 2 (Capture): Complete - PI→LHC event mapping with content-part fan-out, turn derivation (one LHC turn per agent run), parallel tool correlation by toolCallId, error-result capture, graceful abort handling, runtime-change capture (model_select/thinking_level_select), idempotency-keyed dedup, capture-failure isolation.\",\"Story 3 (Verification): Complete - corpus replay through real converter, read-back comparison against fixtures (events/messages/turns/order), deterministic replay verified, inspect overview/health surfaces.\",\"Story 4 (Fork): Complete - fork detection (hook + PI session tree fallback), new thread seeded by replay to fork point, source thread immutability verified, derived forms requeue (v1 correctness, reuse optimization deferred).\",\"Story 5 (Inference): Complete - ModelCall function over PI model registry, multi-lane routing, provider-error classification (auth/invalid_request terminal, rate_limit/timeout/network retryable, thrown→other), empty_output handling by LHC adapter.\",\"Story 6 (Validation): Complete - all seven assignments validated against PI registry before first derivation use, unreachable lane reporting with kind+(provider,model)+fix, headless-safe reporting (ctx.ui.notify when available, stderr fallback), capture continues on validation failure.\"],\"productionPathFindings\":[\"Real LHC SDK execution path confirmed - no LHC mocking, all persistence runs against real SQLite temp threads in tests.\",\"Real converter path exercised - mapMessage, TurnAccumulator, and capture functions are production code, not test doubles.\",\"Real fork seeding path - seedFork uses actual intakeStream.messageEvents for replay, not a mock write path.\",\"Real inspect/health surfaces - overview and health reads come from LHC SDK, not faked responses.\",\"PI types deviation is documented and temporary - local declarations in src/pi/types.ts mirror verified v0.79.2 shapes; will swap to real @earendil-works/pi-coding-agent imports when package is installed (Epic 2/4).\",\"pi-ai types deviation is documented and temporary - local declarations in src/inference/pi-ai.ts; production uses dynamic import of @earendil-works/pi-ai with graceful failure when unavailable.\",\"Deterministic ModelCall fakes in test/fixtures/model-call.ts are appropriate test-boundary instrumentation, not production-path shims.\",\"Observe-only provider in verify/replay.ts is appropriate for verification - it correctly fails derivations rather than fabricating text, matching Epic 1's observe-only contract.\",\"Startup validation warnings about 'unknown_model' during test runs are expected - tests run without a real PI model registry; the validation logic itself correctly probes registry.find/hasConfiguredAuth.\"],\"blockingFindings\":[],\"nonBlockingFindings\":[{\"id\":\"NF-001\",\"severity\":\"observation\",\"title\":\"Documented idempotency edge case for identity-less events\",\"evidence\":\"Story 2 implementation log notes SV-001 residual: a truly identity-less event (no entryId AND no source position AND same content) cannot satisfy both stable-on-redelivery AND unique-per-occurrence constraints. Real PI message_end always carries a stable entry id per research line 142, so this edge is unreachable on the production hook path.\",\"affectedFiles\":[\"packages/pi-lhc/src/capture/idempotency.ts\"],\"requirementIds\":[\"AC-2.6\"],\"recommendedFixScope\":\"human-ruling\",\"blocking\":false},{\"id\":\"NF-002\",\"severity\":\"observation\",\"title\":\"PI extension input/selection API unavailable for --resume picker\",\"evidence\":\"Story 1 implementation log notes SV-002: PI v0.79.2 exposes no interactive input/selection surface. Production --resume presents candidates via ctx.ui.notify and auto-selects most-recent. Exact operator selection and exact-prior-thread reload are deferred until PI provides the API.\",\"affectedFiles\":[\"packages/pi-lhc/src/lifecycle/picker.ts\"],\"requirementIds\":[\"AC-1.7\"],\"recommendedFixScope\":\"fresh-fix-path\",\"blocking\":false},{\"id\":\"NF-003\",\"severity\":\"observation\",\"title\":\"Derived form reuse optimization deferred for v1\",\"evidence\":\"Story 4 fork implementation always requeues derived forms rather than copying/reusing ready forms. Fork correctness is preserved (AC-3.3 permits reuse 'may'), but provenance-identity safety is not yet implemented. Reuse optimization deferred to Epic 2+.\",\"affectedFiles\":[\"packages/pi-lhc/src/lifecycle/fork.ts\"],\"requirementIds\":[\"AC-3.3\"],\"recommendedFixScope\":\"fresh-fix-path\",\"blocking\":false}],\"unresolvedItems\":[\"M0 corpora for Story 3 fixtures - current implementation uses synthetic builders; test coverage widens when M0 delivers recorded PI sessions.\",\"Image/file-reference handling decision (A-7) - interim implementation degrades unsupported parts to runtime_note events with omission text; safe default that can extend intake schema when M0 decides.\",\"PI extension input/selection API - upstream request filed for real --resume picker and exact-thread reload capability.\",\"createSdk→initLhc rename (A-4) - mechanical rename pending in lhc package; pi-lhc uses initLhc wrapper as documented in tech design.\"],\"gateResult\":\"pass\"},{\"resultId\":\"c625f22f-c2c2-4ce8-a2fc-faf4d3d5c617\",\"outcome\":\"block\",\"provider\":\"codex\",\"model\":\"gpt-5.5\",\"reviewerLabel\":\"epic-reviewer-2\",\"crossStoryFindings\":[\"The implemented epic is mostly coherent across Stories 2-6, and the configured Story/Epic gates pass. The remaining cross-story issue is Story 1 thread identity: reload and resume are foundational to every later capture, fork, verification, and derivation flow, so accepting cwd-most-recent behavior changes the meaning of a recorded thread across the whole epic.\"],\"architectureFindings\":[\"AC-1.5 says reload reconstructs from durable state, specifically the resolved thread id. The implementation reattaches no-flag and --resume reloads by cwd-most-recent registry row instead of the prior resolved thread id.\",\"AC-1.7 says --resume resolves the operator's selection. The production path presents candidates through ctx.ui.notify, then auto-selects the most recent thread. The tested production behavior matches that deviation, not the literal acceptance criterion.\",\"No context hook is registered for Epic 1, capture/inference/fork/validation modules are wired through real LHC surfaces, and tests exercise temp SQLite threads rather than mocked src modules.\"],\"epicCoverageAssessment\":[\"Flow 1 is partially covered but blocked on AC-1.5 and AC-1.7 production behavior.\",\"Flows 2, 3, 4, 5, and 6 have direct source/tests and latest story-verifier evidence showing pass, including capture gaps, fork replay, model-call routing, startup validation, and replay/inspect verification.\",\"The M0 corpus breadth remains a named spec input; current replay fixtures are synthetic/fixture-backed but the Story 3 implementation drives the real converter and intake path.\"],\"productionPathFindings\":[\"Material production-path finding: reload for no-flag and --resume uses cwd-most-recent registry selection, which can attach capture to the wrong thread when more than one thread exists for the cwd.\",\"Material production-path finding: production --resume has no real operator selection path; it notifies the list and auto-selects most recent.\",\"No material fake model adapter or fabricated completion path remains in production inference: createModelCall resolves through PI modelRegistry and dynamically imports @earendil-works/pi-ai, returning classified failures if unavailable. Test fakes are confined to test fixtures.\"],\"blockingFindings\":[{\"id\":\"EV-001\",\"severity\":\"major\",\"title\":\"Reload can reattach to the wrong cwd thread\",\"evidence\":\"Epic AC-1.5 requires reload reconstruction from the resolved thread id (docs/specs/02-pi-lhc/01-connector-core/epic.md:137). resolveReloadThread documents no-flag/--resume reload as cwd-most-recent and returns listed.value.at(-1) (packages/pi-lhc/src/lifecycle/thread-resolution.ts:118, packages/pi-lhc/src/lifecycle/thread-resolution.ts:141). The production test proves only the single-thread cwd case (packages/pi-lhc/test/lifecycle/thread-resolution.test.ts:335). Latest Story 1 verifier also marked this needs-human-ruling in artifacts/01-session-lifecycle-and-thread-resolution/014-verify.json.\",\"affectedFiles\":[\"packages/pi-lhc/src/lifecycle/thread-resolution.ts\",\"packages/pi-lhc/src/index.ts\",\"packages/pi-lhc/test/lifecycle/thread-resolution.test.ts\",\"docs/specs/02-pi-lhc/01-connector-core/artifacts/01-session-lifecycle-and-thread-resolution/014-verify.json\"],\"requirementIds\":[\"AC-1.5\",\"TC-1.5\"],\"recommendedFixScope\":\"human-ruling\",\"blocking\":true},{\"id\":\"EV-002\",\"severity\":\"major\",\"title\":\"Production --resume does not resolve an operator selection\",\"evidence\":\"Epic AC-1.7 requires --resume to resolve the operator's selection (docs/specs/02-pi-lhc/01-connector-core/epic.md:141). defaultSelectThread states PI lacks an interactive selection surface, notifies candidates, then returns mostRecent.threadId (packages/pi-lhc/src/index.ts:181, packages/pi-lhc/src/index.ts:195). The production test asserts the most-recent default as the selected thread (packages/pi-lhc/test/lifecycle/thread-resolution.test.ts:255, packages/pi-lhc/test/lifecycle/thread-resolution.test.ts:289). Latest Story 1 verifier marked this needs-human-ruling in artifacts/01-session-lifecycle-and-thread-resolution/014-verify.json.\",\"affectedFiles\":[\"packages/pi-lhc/src/index.ts\",\"packages/pi-lhc/src/lifecycle/picker.ts\",\"packages/pi-lhc/test/lifecycle/thread-resolution.test.ts\",\"docs/specs/02-pi-lhc/01-connector-core/artifacts/01-session-lifecycle-and-thread-resolution/014-verify.json\"],\"requirementIds\":[\"AC-1.7\",\"TC-1.7\"],\"recommendedFixScope\":\"human-ruling\",\"blocking\":true}],\"nonBlockingFindings\":[],\"unresolvedItems\":[\"Human ruling needed: accept or reject cwd-most-recent reload reattach for no-flag/--resume launches.\",\"Human ruling needed: accept or reject notify-list plus most-recent default as the v1 production --resume behavior until PI exposes an interactive selection API.\"],\"gateResult\":\"pass\"}]},\"errors\":[],\"warnings\":[],\"artifacts\":[{\"kind\":\"result-envelope\",\"path\":\"/Users/leemoore/code/pi-long-horizon/liminal-context/docs/specs/02-pi-lhc/01-connector-core/artifacts/epic/001-epic-review.json\"}],\"startedAt\":\"2026-06-14T13:37:31.599Z\",\"finishedAt\":\"2026-06-14T13:41:35.098Z\"}\n2\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"a7689c21-1739-4f71-b1a5-e967f006f0f9","uuid":"b2abe083-ed94-4f97-b834-bd2164fccacb","timestamp":"2026-06-14T13:45:52.802Z","tool_use_result":{"type":"text","file":{"filePath":"/Users/leemoore/code/pi-long-horizon/liminal-context/docs/specs/02-pi-lhc/01-connector-core/artifacts/epic/001-epic-review.json","content":"{\"command\":\"epic-review\",\"version\":1,\"status\":\"blocked\",\"outcome\":\"block\",\"result\":{\"outcome\":\"block\",\"canonicalReview\":{\"outcome\":\"block\",\"reviewerLabels\":[\"epic-reviewer-1\",\"epic-reviewer-2\"],\"reconciliationSummary\":\"Reviewer-1 assessed the epic as complete with three non-blocking observations about documented limitations. Reviewer-2 identified two major blocking findings (EV-001, EV-002) concerning Story 1 thread identity on reload and --resume operator selection. Both findings are supported by code evidence: the implementation explicitly acknowledges cwd-most-recent reload reattach as an Epic-1 convenience with concurrent same-cwd limitations (thread-resolution.ts:118-121) and most-recent auto-selection as a spec deviation due to PI's lack of interactive input (index.ts:181-190). The Story 1 verification artifact (014-verify.json) confirms both SV-001 and SV-002 are 'needs-human-ruling' with gates passing but production behavior deviating from literal AC requirements. Because Reviewer-2 returned block and the deviations are acknowledged in-code with no human-ruling accepting them, the conservative position preserves the block.\",\"crossStoryFindings\":[\"Cross-story consistency is strong across Stories 2-6. The plain-data-only rule (AC-1.3) is consistently enforced — only SessionState is 