{"type":"assistant","message":{"id":"msg_202606142146527eb4199106764d11","type":"message","role":"assistant","model":"glm-4.7","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"Now I have the complete picture. Let me verify the two blocking issues directly from the code:\n\n**EV-001 / SV-001: Reload reconstruction uses cwd-most-recent instead of resolved thread id**\n\nLooking at `thread-resolution.ts` lines 131-148 (`resolveReloadThread` function):\n- For `--session` and `--continue`, it re-resolves by launch input (which is correct)\n- For `no-flag` and `--resume` (which map to `--resume` picker), it lists threads by cwd and selects the most recent (`listed.value.at(-1)`)\n\nThe comment at lines 118-121 explicitly states:\n```\n// - no flag or `--resume`: reattach to the cwd's most-recently-created thread,\n//   read from the registry. A no-flag Story-1 session created exactly one thread\n//   in its cwd, so that is the thread; re-running the launch instead would create\n//   a duplicate (no flag) or re-prompt the operator (`--resume`).\n```\n\nThis confirms EV-001: The implementation uses cwd-most-recent registry selection, not reconstruction from the resolved thread id. The code acknowledges this as an Epic-1 convenience with known concurrent same-cwd limitations.\n\n**EV-002 / SV-002: Production --resume auto-selects most recent instead of operator selection**\n\nLooking at `index.ts` lines 210-227 (`defaultSelectThread` function):\n```typescript\nfunction defaultSelectThread(\n  choices: readonly ThreadChoice[],\n  ctx: ExtensionContext,\n): Promise<string | null> {\n  if (ctx.hasUI) {\n    ctx.ui.notify(renderResumeCandidates(choices), { level: choices.length === 1 ? \"info\" : \"warn\" });\n  }\n  return Promise.resolve(choices.length === 1 ? choices[0]?.threadId ?? null : null);\n}\n```\n\nThe implementation presents candidates through `ctx.ui.notify` but auto-selects only when there's exactly one candidate. With multiple candidates, it returns `null` and directs the operator to use `--session <id>` explicitly. The comment acknowledges PI v0.79.2 lacks an interactive selection API.\n\nBoth findings are confirmed by the code and match what the epic review reported. No formal ruling exists for Story 1, and the issues remain \"needs-human-ruling\" with gates passing.\n\nSince these are the only blockers and the epic review correctly identified them, my assessment is \"blocked\" pending human ruling on these two documented deviations.\n\nThe non-blocking findings (NF-001 idempotency edge case, NF-002 picker API limitation, NF-003 fork form reuse) should remain separate since they're observations rather than blockers. No new issues surfaced since the review—fix batch 001 doesn't exist, so nothing has changed.","signature":""}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":0,"output_tokens":0},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"a7689c21-1739-4f71-b1a5-e967f006f0f9","uuid":"039911b0-096a-42c4-b3be-c3d14673e50a"}
