{"type":"assistant","message":{"id":"msg_202606142146527eb4199106764d11","type":"message","role":"assistant","model":"glm-4.7","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Based on my independent verification of the code and artifacts, I can now provide my assessment. The two blocking findings from the epic review are confirmed by the current code:\n\n**EV-001 / SV-001 confirmed**: In `thread-resolution.ts:131-148`, `resolveReloadThread` for no-flag and --resume uses `threads.listThreads({ cwd })` and selects `listed.value.at(-1)` (the most recent). The comment explicitly acknowledges this as an \"Epic-1 convenience\" with \"known concurrent same-cwd limitation.\"\n\n**EV-002 / SV-002 confirmed**: In `index.ts:219-227`, `defaultSelectThread` presents candidates via `ctx.ui.notify` but auto-selects only when single, returning `null` for multiple. The comment explicitly states PI v0.79.2 \"exposes no interactive input/selection surface.\"\n\n**Key findings**:\n- No fix-batch artifact exists (no post-epic-review fixes)\n- No human-ruling artifact exists for Story 1 (unlike Stories 0 and 4)\n- The verification artifact (014-verify.json) still shows \"needs-human-ruling\"\n- Gates pass but deviations are documented\n- These are platform-constrained deviations (PI API limitations), not code defects\n\n```json\n{\n  \"outcome\": \"blocked\",\n  \"confirmedIssues\": [\n    \"EV-001: Reload for no-flag and --resume uses cwd-most-recent registry selection instead of reconstructing from the resolved thread id (AC-1.5). Implementation acknowledges this as an Epic-1 convenience with concurrent same-cwd limitation; no human-ruling artifact exists accepting this deviation.\",\n    \"EV-002: Production --resume auto-selects most recent thread instead of resolving an operator selection (AC-1.7). Implementation acknowledges PI v0.79.2 lacks interactive input/selection surface; no human-ruling artifact exists accepting this deviation.\"\n  ],\n  \"disputedOrUnconfirmedIssues\": [],\n  \"readinessAssessment\": \"Epic remains blocked on two Story 1 deviations that require human ruling. Code evidence confirms both issues as documented. Gates pass but these are spec deviations, not test failures. No fix-batch or ruling artifacts exist to address these post-epic-review. The deviations stem from PI platform API constraints (no interactive selection surface), not implementation defects. Independent verification confirms the canonical review's findings remain current.\",\n  \"recommendedNextStep\": \"Provide human ruling on EV-001 and EV-002. Both deviations are documented in code and verification artifacts with acknowledged limitations. If accepted, create ruling artifacts accepting these as platform-constrained deviations (similar to Story 0 and Story 4 ruling patterns). The impl-lead previously accepted these under standing authorization per team-impl-log.md, but no formal ruling document exists.\"\n}\n```"}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":0,"output_tokens":0},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"a7689c21-1739-4f71-b1a5-e967f006f0f9","uuid":"7f15c422-b679-41c8-a8a5-3bc13fad17cd"}
